                    <p>
                        Most breweries have a story behind every beer. Sometimes the story has a mission and can help
                        build your breweries mission, or sometimes it’s a goof and can simply create a point of
                        discussion amongst your local community. No matter the purpose, my process begins by
                        understanding how the idea came to light and asking
                    </p>
                    <p class="callout">
                        “How can we make this more than just a beer label?
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Over the years I’ve explored, designed, and launched beers with all types of artwork styles.
                        From characters and mascots to landscapes. Pattern heavy designs to simple iconography. Detailed
                        line-work to letter heavy designs. I helped build sub-brands such as “Don’t Fuck It Up!”, a low
                        impact ale that bring awareness to water conservation efforts, and “Dirty Hop Water”, a series
                        devoted entirely to the music that fuels
                        the brew team.
                        <br><br>
                        Regardless of the style or purpose, the artwork is always in vector format, ensuring that either
                        the artwork, pattern, word-mark, or iconography can easily be repurposed for
                        merchandising.
                        <br><br>

                        The creativity within the craft beer industry goes hand in hand with illustrative design or
                        collaborating with artists, and if you are a brewpub who does not need to fight for shelf space,
                        you have the opportunity to ensure your beer label should are as unique as your beers.

                    </p>

